  "notes": "This corrective slice closes a fail-open in the merged VerificationStateHistory consumer. A later recorded transition may be effective before its own recorded time, but it cannot be effective before the parent transition it replaces. Without that dependency closure, replay could select an ACTIVE re-verification while its parent revocation was not yet effective. The repair adds a stable semantic finding, defensive replay ancestry enforcement, exact-negative fixtures in both canonical and resolver lanes, regression tests, and direct documentation. It does not change schemas, source admission, policy evaluation, public projection, lifecycle state, release, deployment, publication, or repository settings. Rollback is a normal revert of this correction commit; the merged history-aware resolver remains otherwise intact."
